This paper investigates a nonlocal biharmonic differential equation, specifically \begin{align*}
\begin{split}
\Delta^2u+\beta\Delta u= &\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|}u_x\right)*\left(\frac{1}{|x|}u_x\right)\\
&+ \left(\frac{1}{|x|^{\mu}}u_x\right)*\left(\frac{1}{|x|^{\mu}}u_x\right)\frac{1}{|x|^{\mu}}\left(\frac{1-|x|^{2m}}{e^{-\gamma |x|^{2m}}-1\ } \right),
\end{split}
\end{align*}
where $\lambda$ and $\beta$ are positive constants, $\mu$ is either equal to $2\pi$ or less than $2m$, and the final term on the right-hand side involves the function $h(x)=\frac{1-|x|^{2m}}{e^{-\gamma |x|^{2m}}-1\ }$. We utilize Trudinger-Moser inequality to establish that the given equation possesses ground solutions when $\lambda$ is less than or equal to the first eigenvalue of $\Delta^2 -\beta\Delta$.

