The paper provides proofs of uniform solutions to a class of sub-quadratic, non-autonomous barrier equations in R^n. These proofs contribute to understanding the solutions to a category of non-autonomous barrier issues of the type:
\begin{equation}
\begin{cases}
\min\left\{\lambda(k(x,t),d_u\phi,\partial_t\phi+\mathcal{M}^+(b(x,t),D_x\phi)),\mathcal{I}(x,t,d_u\phi,\partial_t\phi)\right\}=0,\\
(x,t)\in\Omega\times(0,T).
\end{cases
\end{equation}

With these proofs known, the knowledge for uniform solutions to a category of non-autonomous barrier issues is substantially developed. To achieve this, no major assumptions are made regarding the sub-quadratic expansion condition.
